        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "97934246-b3d1-59ab-9c4a-f9b05f4d6956",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Lush, P.O.D.\n- People: Miki Berenyi, Emma Anderson, Phil King, Chris Acland, Sonny Sandoval, Wuv Bernardo, Marcos Curiel, Traa Daniels\n- Albums and songs: Gala, Goodbye for Now, Testify\n- Places: London, San Diego, California\n- Companies: 4AD\n\nFacts:\n- Lush were an English rock band formed in London in 1987.\n- Gala is the debut compilation album by Lush, released in 1990 by 4AD for the US and Japanese markets and made up of Lush's earliest releases in reverse chronological order plus two additional tracks.\n- P.O.D. is a Christian nu metal band formed in 1992 and based in San Diego, California.\n- Goodbye for Now is a song by P.O.D. and the lead single from the band's sixth studio album, Testify, released in 2006.\n- Before Lush's original split, the band's lineup consisted of Miki Berenyi, Emma Anderson, Phil King, and Chris Acland.\n- The P.O.D. lineup consists of Sonny Sandoval, Wuv Bernardo, Marcos Curiel, and Traa Daniels.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "43aaed45-5a6d-5cc5-a174-7f073df3af44",
        "text": "Page: Lush (band). Sentence: Lush were an English rock band formed in London in 1987.\nPage: Lush (band). Sentence: The lineup before the original split consisted of Miki Berenyi (vocals, guitar), Emma Anderson (vocals, guitar), Phil King (bass) and Chris Acland (drums).\nPage: P.O.D.. Sentence: Payable on Death (abbreviated P.O.D.) is a Christian nu metal band formed in 1992 and based in San Diego, California.\nPage: P.O.D.. Sentence: The band's line-up consists of vocalist Sonny Sandoval, drummer Wuv Bernardo, guitarist Marcos Curiel, and bassist Traa Daniels.\nPage: Gala (album). Sentence: Gala is the debut compilation album by the English alternative rock band Lush, released in 1990 by 4AD as an introduction to the US and Japanese markets, comprising the band's earliest releases in reverse chronological order, plus two additional tracks.\nPage: Goodbye for Now (song). Sentence: \"Goodbye for Now\" is a song by P.O.D. and the lead single from their sixth studio album, \"Testify\", released in 2006.",
